;; view/glon/theme_lib.glon -- reusable VID themes (the VID design tokens).
;;
;; Themes are ordinary Glon data.  Widgets read colours, metrics and flags from
;; the selected theme; no widget policy is in C.
;;
;; Slot map (block-at theme N).  A colour is four slots r g b a starting at N,
;; so colour slots are always 1 + 4k.  Reading at any other index mixes two
;; colours (the cause of the pre-WG-3 green text and red focus blocks).
;;
;;   0 dark/light flag       1 window background     5 pane surface
;;   9 primary text         13 accent              17 border
;;  21 input background     25 input text          29 secondary text
;;  33 hover surface        37 raised / header      41 accent hover
;;  45 accent pressed       49 disabled surface     53 table selection
;;  57 table focus          61 shadow               65 highlight
;;  69 body font            70 small font           71 padding  72 gap
;;  73 selected row         77 clear                81 text on accent
;;  85 accent subtle        89 sunken (code) bg     93 disabled text
;;  97 danger              101 danger hover        105 focus ring
;; 109 control surface     113 control hover       117 control pressed
;; 121 heading text        125 divider             129 alternate row
;; 133 heading font        134 title font
;; INTENT-4B-5A metrics (read by VID and Intent; a look may change them):
;; 135 border width (px)     136 corner radius (px)
;; 137 font style (bit 0 bold; bits 1-2 family: 0 sans, 1 serif, 2 monospace)
;; 138 control height (px)   139 control width (px, 0 = from the content)
;;
;; Contrast (INTENT-4B-5A, WCAG 2 ratios, checked by test_gui_p2 theme-contrast):
;; text on every surface >= 4.5; text on accent / danger >= 4.5; borders,
;; focus ring and the checked box against their surfaces >= 3; disabled text
;; on the disabled surface >= 3.  The dark theme keeps its look; only its
;; borders, accent, disabled text and pressed surface were corrected.
[
